      "writtenOn": "2025-11-10T20:51:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think we should include the lineHeight setting, for a few reasons:\n\n1) This is a text block, and an appropriate leading should be built into the font already.\n2) This is intended to appear exactly like a terminal, and they traditionally do not have added leading.\n3) Changing this is likely to negatively affect the rendering of non-textual elements (ie, ascii art, etc).\n\nIncidentally, I don\u0027t think the WCAG spec is saying: set line height to 1.5x font size for maximum accessibility.  I think it says: to avoid encumbering accessibility, ensure that if a user uses an accessibility tool to set the line height to 1.5x there is no reduction in functionality.  I think we\u0027re good.",
      "parentUuid": "98d5d1fe_8eb20ec0",
      "revId": "0c9396c2ef6df6a1ef5c7df0cc18011c9e40aa41",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
